NNAAMMEE
       e2scrub_all - check all mounted ext[234] file systems for errors.

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ee22ssccrruubb__aallll [[OOPPTTIIOONN]]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Searches  the  system  for  all LVM logical volumes containing an ext2,
       ext3, or ext4 file system, and checks them for problems.  The  checking
       is  performed by invoking the ee22ssccrruubb tool, which will look for corrup‐
       tions.  Corrupt file systems will be tagged as having  errors  so  that
       fsck  will  be invoked before the next mount.  If no errors are encoun‐
       tered, ffssttrriimm will be called on the file system if it is mounted.   See
       the  ee22ssccrruubb manual page for more information about how the checking is
       performed.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --nn     Print what commands ee22ssccrruubb__aallll would execute  to  initiate  the
              e2scrub  operations.  (Note: these commands will not actually be
              executed; however, since ee22ssccrruubb__aallll needs  to  run  some  addi‐
              tional,  privileged  commands  to  query the system to determine
              which ee22ssccrruubb commands would be executed, it still needs  to  be
              run as root.)

       --rr     Remove e2scrub snapshots but do not check anything.

       --AA     Scrub all ext[234] file systems even if they are not mounted.

       --VV     Print version information and exit.

